Bluetooth: hci_qca: power WCN3950 off like the other WCN399x

WCN3950 was added to the WCN399x cases of the power-on and setup paths
but not to qca_power_off() and qca_serdev_remove(): closing hci0 sent no
power-off pulse and left the regulators on, so the controller kept running
the patch it had downloaded. The next open (bluetoothd powering it, or
setting the public address) then reran the setup on a patched controller,
whose answer to the first TLV segment is not the expected one:

  Bluetooth: hci0: QCA TLV response size mismatch
  Bluetooth: hci0: QCA Failed to request file: qca/cmbtfw13.tlv (-84)
  Bluetooth: hci0: Retry BT power ON:0..2

and hci0 stayed unconfigured. Handle WCN3950 like WCN3988/3990/3991/3998.

--- a/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/hci_qca.c
@@ -2247,6 +2247,7 @@
 	power = qcadev->bt_power;
 
 	switch (soc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3950:
 	case QCA_WCN3988:
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
@@ -2271,6 +2272,7 @@
         }
 
 	switch (soc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3950:
 	case QCA_WCN3988:
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
@@ -2582,6 +2584,7 @@
 	struct qca_power *power = qcadev->bt_power;
 
 	switch (qcadev->btsoc_type) {
+	case QCA_WCN3950:
 	case QCA_WCN3988:
 	case QCA_WCN3990:
 	case QCA_WCN3991:
